From 19317229d2fed6c8d42476fe35f44a9914a30f68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StachowiakDawid <dawidos234@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:38:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: samsung: add an Exynos 9820 CSIS RAW capture driver

V4L2 capture driver for the MIPI CSI-2 receivers of the Exynos 9820
with their write DMA: RAW Bayer frames from the sensor straight to
memory, one video node per receiver.

 - D-PHY/C-PHY combo PHY setup with the vendor settle table; split PHY
   for CSIS3_1.
 - Works with the screen off: the MIF/INT DVFS levels are held while
   streaming. Drives the MIPI switch; one stream at a time.
 - Extra virtual channels; sub-device nodes are registered late.
 - Robust stream stop: the write DMA is aborted on errors and at
   stream stop, a wedged DMA is detected, the ISPPRE bus divider is
   written at every stream start, and a block that is not fully
   powered is never touched.
 - cmu_option: bits set in the CMU_ISPPRE controller option register
   at stream start (default none; the power domain driver restores
   the register).
 - The receiver state is logged at stream start and stop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
